   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# LTXE HDR Native EXR (experimental)\n\n**HDR in, HDR out.** An EXR plate (already scene-linear) is refined by the official **LTX-2.5 general-refine IC-LoRA**\n(ComfyUI-LTXVideo) and written as **ACEScg EXR** frames numbered by source frame. This is NOT the SDR-to-HDR\nconversion: for SDR video use *LTXE_SDR_to_HDR_Pro*.\n\n**Before you run**\n1. Install **ComfyUI-LTXVideo** (Lightricks) and its requirements (colour-science, OpenImageIO).\n2. Put the LTX-2.5 files where the loaders look (official names; links in the ComfyUI-LTXVideo README). The LTX-2\n   licence terms apply to the weights.\n3. In *Load EXR sequence* set the folder of `*.exr` frames, its colour space (`srgb_linear` = scene-linear Rec.709,\n   `acescg`, or `acescct`) and the frame rate.\n\n**Long plates:** run with `window` = 0, read the plan, then raise `window` by 1 per run. Frames land at\n`output/ltxe_hdr_native/<shot>/<shot>_1001.exr ...`.\n\nThe prompt is encoded locally (CLIPTextEncode). The official graph's GemmaAPITextEncode is a paid API and is not used.\nNothing here has been run with the real model in this repository (needs a GPU); treat results as experimental.\n"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# LTXE HDR Native EXR (experimental)\n\n**HDR in, HDR out.** An EXR plate (already scene-linear) is refined by the official **LTX-2.5 general-refine IC-LoRA**\n(ComfyUI-LTXVideo) and written as **ACEScg EXR** frames numbered by source frame. This is NOT the SDR-to-HDR\nconversion: for SDR video use *LTXE_SDR_to_HDR_Pro*.\n\n**Before you run**\n1. Install **ComfyUI-LTXVideo** (Lightricks) and its requirements (colour-science, OpenImageIO).\n2. Put the LTX-2.5 files where the loaders look (official names; links in the ComfyUI-LTXVideo README). The LTX-2\n   licence terms apply to the weights.\n3. In *Load EXR sequence* set the folder of `*.exr` frames, its colour space (`srgb_linear` = scene-linear Rec.709,\n   `acescg`, or `acescct`) and the frame rate.\n\n**Long plates:** run with `window` = 0, read the plan, then raise `window` by 1 per run. Frames land at\n`output/ltxe_hdr_native/<shot>/<shot>_1001.exr ...`.\n\nThe prompt is encoded locally (CLIPTextEncode). The official graph's GemmaAPITextEncode is a paid API and is not used.\nNothing here has been run with the real model in this repository (needs a GPU); treat results as experimental.\n"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
